---
title: "3 · Pick services and prices"
description: Add packages and services to an opportunity and agree the prices.
sidebar:
  order: 4
  label: "3 · Pick services and prices"
---

**Who:** the person in charge of the opportunity. **Where:** the opportunity › **Services** tab.

{% steps %}

1. Open the opportunity and go to the **Services** tab. The country comes from the opportunity; only the items offered in that country can be added.
2. Select **Add packages and services**. The catalog opens as its own view.
3. Choose a group (**Packages** or a category), search, or filter by **Department**, and select **Add** on a package or a single service. The agreed price starts at the catalog price. The catalog stays open, so several items can be added in a row.
4. Select **← Back to services**.
5. Change **Qty** or **Agreed** where needed. The totals and the discount against the catalog (**vs catalog**) are updated as you type.

{% /steps %}

{% screenshot id="crm/services-list" caption="The packages and services offered in the opportunity's country." /%}

## The catalog view

The **Add packages and services** view groups the items: **Packages**, then one group for each category, then **Other**. Select a group to list its items, or search by name or code across every group. Each row shows the code, category, department, billing and reference price of the item. The **Department** filter narrows the list to one department.

- Select the arrow on a package to expand it and see the services it includes.
- A service that is already included in a package on the opportunity cannot be added on its own, and a package that includes a service already on the opportunity cannot be added. The row says why.
- A service marked **Missing contract text** has no wording yet for this country in that language. Generation of a contract in that language stops on it. Ask the department lead to add the text under **Services & Packages** (see [2 · Services & Packages](/en/crm/services-packages/)).

{% screenshot id="crm/services-filter-department" caption="Filtering the list by department." /%}

{% screenshot id="crm/services-package-expanded" caption="A package expanded to show the services it includes." /%}

{% aside type="note" title="Prices are changed only here" %}
The **Services** tab is the only place where the services and prices of a deal are changed. Once the opportunity has contracts, the opportunity's amount is the total of every contract that is not void.
{% /aside %}

{% screenshot id="crm/services-added" caption="Services added at the catalog price." /%}

{% screenshot id="crm/services-agreed-discount" caption="Agreed prices lowered to 20% below the catalog price." /%}

## The services table

Besides the price columns, each row shows its **Contract** and **Contract status** (**Not in a contract**, **Draft**, **Sent** or **Signed**). Once a contract is signed, the **Delivery**, **Next invoice** and **Next work due** columns follow the delivery of each signed service (see [11 · Delivery after signing](/en/crm/delivery/)).

## Services in a signed contract are locked

A row in a signed contract cannot be changed or removed: its quantity and price are shown as text, with the contract number. To stop such a service, end it on the contract (see [11 · Delivery after signing](/en/crm/delivery/)). To sell more, add the new services here and make an add-on contract for them (see [8 · Paper signing, void and copy](/en/crm/paper-void-copy/)).

{% screenshot id="crm/services-signed-locked" caption="Services in a signed contract: read-only, with the contract number and status." /%}

## Example

An opportunity for ABC PTE. LTD. in Singapore needs an annual bookkeeping service and a GST filing service. The person in charge adds both at the catalog price, then lowers the agreed prices by 20% as agreed with the client. The **vs catalog** figure in the totals row shows the discount on the total.
